FREECIV PATCH — Monte Carlo reseed on load
===========================================

Target file: server/savegame/savegame3.c
Target function: sg_load_random

After restoring the saved RNG state via fc_rand_set_state(), check for
/tmp/freeciv_reseed. If it contains an integer, call fc_srand() with that
value to overwrite the restored state with a fresh fc_srand(seed) state.
Delete the file so each load uses it at most once.

This enables Monte Carlo rollouts: start with one savegame, write N
different seed values to /tmp/freeciv_reseed between loads, get N
different futures from the same saved state.

Original sg_load_random (in `random.saved=TRUE` branch):

    loading->rstate.is_init = TRUE;
    fc_rand_set_state(loading->rstate);

Patched sg_load_random:

    loading->rstate.is_init = TRUE;
    fc_rand_set_state(loading->rstate);

    /* CIVBENCH MC reseed hook: if /tmp/freeciv_reseed exists, treat its
     * contents as an unsigned integer and reseed via fc_srand(). The file
     * is consumed (deleted) so it only applies to one load. */
    {
      FILE *fp = fopen("/tmp/freeciv_reseed", "r");
      if (fp != NULL) {
        unsigned long mc_seed = 0;
        if (fscanf(fp, "%lu", &mc_seed) == 1) {
          log_normal("CIVBENCH: reseeding RNG via fc_srand(%lu)", mc_seed);
          fc_srand((RANDOM_TYPE) mc_seed);
          loading->rstate = fc_rand_state();
        }
        fclose(fp);
        (void) unlink("/tmp/freeciv_reseed");
      }
    }
